---
config:
  layout: elk
---
classDiagram
    direction LR
    class Main {
        +run_vsr_mcts()
        +run_mcts()
        +configure_grammar()
    }
    class Equation_evaluator {
        +get_nvars()
        +get_vars_range_and_types()
        +evaluate()
        +compute_metric()
    }

    class DataX {
        +sample()
        +vars_range_and_types
    }
    class RegressTask {
        +rand_draw_data_with_X_fixed()
        +evaluate()
        +set_allowed_inputs()
        +oracle
        +dataX
    }

    class Program {
        +optimize()
        +evalaute_loss()
        +set_vf()
        +free_var_mask
    }
    class ProductionRules {
        <<module>>
        +get_production_rules()
        +get_var_i_production_rules()
        +base_grammar
        +augmented_grammars
    }
    class Utils {
        <<module>>
        +create_uniform_generations()
        +create_reward_threshold()
        +pretty_print_expr()
        +expression_to_template()
        +nth_repl()
    }
    class MCTS {
        +step()
        +freeze_equations()
        +task
        +program
    }
    Main --> Equation_evaluator : instantiates
    Equation_evaluator --> DataX : exposes ranges
    Main --> DataX : configures
    Main --> RegressTask : wraps
    Main --> Program : constructs
    Main --> MCTS : builds
    Main --> ProductionRules : selects
    Main --> Utils : schedules
    RegressTask --> Equation_evaluator : evaluate (labels/metrics)
    MCTS --> RegressTask : rand_draw_data_with_X_fixed (draw batches)
    MCTS --> Program : optimize, evalaute_loss (score rollouts)
    Program --> Equation_evaluator : compute_metric (loss metric)
    MCTS ..> RegressTask : set_allowed_inputs (update allowed inputs)
    MCTS ..> Program : set_vf (control variable mask)
    MCTS ..> MCTS : freeze_equations (augment grammar)
    MCTS --> ProductionRules : expand rules
    Program --> Utils : pretty_print_expr (report expressions)
    MCTS --> Utils : expression_to_template, nth_repl (module templating)

    note for ProductionRules "Provided by production_rules.py, production_rules_trigometric.py, and production_rules_feynman.py."
    note for Utils "Utilities in utils.py for schedules, pretty-printing, and module templating."